# WN22-SO-000050: Windows Server 2022 must force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000050-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings.`
    description `Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. This setting allows administrators to enable more precise au`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-mla-let`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,NIST-800-53:AU-12`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-LET`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-LET by setting registry value 'SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_AU_12 `Windows Server implements AU-12 by setting registry value 'SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa`
        name `SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
